   "source": [
    "# 🫀 IoMT ECG Heart Disease Detection: Advanced Training Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "This Jupyter Notebook implements an automated machine learning and deep learning classification pipeline for heart disease detection based on ECG images. The architecture maps perfectly to the requested academic pipeline:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Stage 1 (Dataset Selection)**: Loads the 4-class Kaggle ECG dataset:\n",
    "   * `normal_ecg_images` (Normal)\n",
    "   * `abnormal_heartbeat_ecg_images` (Abnormal)\n",
    "   * `myocardial_infarction_ecg_images` (Myocardial Infarction / MI)\n",
    "   * `post_mi_history_ecg_images` (History of MI)\n",
    "2. **Stage 2 (Image Preprocessing)**: Converts ECGs to grayscale, applies Gaussian smoothing, enhances grid-line contrast using **CLAHE (Contrast Limited Adaptive Histogram Equalization)**, and normalizes pixels.\n",
    "3. **Stage 3 (CNN Backbone Feature Extraction)**: Extracts continuous **2048-dimensional deep feature embeddings** from the pre-trained **InceptionV3** network (the Pakistan ECG paper champion with 93% baseline!).\n",
    "4. **Stage 4 (WSO-LDA Feature Selection)**: Employs **Binary White Shark Optimization (WSO)** coupled with **Linear Discriminant Analysis (LDA)** as a multi-objective fitness function to reduce the feature vector size down to the most significant discriminative subset.\n",
    "5. **Stage 5 (MOSHO-HANN Classification)**: Feeds the selected features into a **Hybrid Artificial Neural Network (HANN)** whose neural weights are optimized via **Multi-Objective Spotted Hyena Optimization (MOSHO)** to maximize diagnostic accuracy and minimize False Negatives.\n",
    "6. **ONNX Export**: Bundles the entire end-to-end pipeline and exports it directly to **ONNX format (`ecg_model.onnx`)** for immediate cross-platform integration into your FastAPI backend!"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 🛠️ Install necessary dependencies\n",
    "# Uncomment and run this cell if you are training on Google Colab or Kaggle!\n",
    "# !pip install torch torchvision scikit-learn onnx onnxruntime opencv-python pillow numpy matplotlib"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📦 1. Imports and Configurations"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import time\n",
    "import copy\n",
    "import cv2\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "import torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from PIL import Image\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n",
    "from torchvision import models, transforms\n",
    "from sklearn.discriminant_analysis import LinearDiscriminantAnalysis\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, recall_score, f1_score\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Set Random Seeds for reproducibility\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(42)\n",
    "if torch.cuda.is_available():\n",
    "    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "print(f\"Using accelerator device: {DEVICE}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🖼️ 2. ECG Preprocessing Pipeline (Grayscale, Gaussian Blur & CLAHE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def preprocess_ecg_image(image_path):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Stage 2: Advanced image cleaning, grayscaling, and CLAHE contrast enhancement\n",
    "    to isolate ECG electrical waveforms from paper grids.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    # Read image using OpenCV\n",
    "    img = cv2.imread(image_path)\n",
    "    if img is None:\n",
    "        return None\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 1. Convert to Grayscale\n",
    "    gray = cv2.cvtColor(img, cv2.COLOR_BGR2GRAY)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 2. Denoise with Gaussian Blur\n",
    "    blurred = cv2.GaussianBlur(gray, (3, 3), 0)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 3. Enhance ECG signal contrast using CLAHE\n",
    "    clahe = cv2.createCLAHE(clipLimit=2.0, tileGridSize=(8, 8))\n",
    "    enhanced = clahe.apply(blurred)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 4. Resize to 224x224 (Standard dimensions for ImageNet CNN models)\n",
    "    resized = cv2.resize(enhanced, (224, 224))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Convert back to 3-channel RGB for InceptionV3 compatibility\n",
    "    rgb_enhanced = cv2.cvtColor(resized, cv2.COLOR_GRAY2RGB)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    return rgb_enhanced\n",
    "\n",
    "# Quick visualization check on the dataset\n",
    "sample_dir = \"ecg_data/normal_ecg_images\"\n",
    "if os.path.exists(sample_dir):\n",
    "    files = os.listdir(sample_dir)\n",
    "    if len(files) > 0:\n",
    "        sample_path = os.path.join(sample_dir, files[0])\n",
    "        enhanced_img = preprocess_ecg_image(sample_path)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        plt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\n",
    "        plt.subplot(1, 2, 1)\n",
    "        plt.title(\"Original ECG\")\n",
    "        plt.imshow(cv2.imread(sample_path)[:,:,::-1])\n",
    "        plt.subplot(1, 2, 2)\n",
    "        plt.title(\"Grayscale + Blurred + CLAHE\")\n",
    "        plt.imshow(enhanced_img)\n",
    "        plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📁 3. PyTorch Custom Dataset"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class ECGDataset(Dataset):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, data_dir, transform=None):\n",
    "        self.data_dir = data_dir\n",
    "        self.transform = transform\n",
    "        self.classes = [\n",
    "            \"normal_ecg_images\",\n",
    "            \"abnormal_heartbeat_ecg_images\",\n",
    "            \"myocardial_infarction_ecg_images\",\n",
    "            \"post_mi_history_ecg_images\"\n",
    "        ]\n",
    "        self.image_paths = []\n",
    "        self.labels = []\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for idx, cls in enumerate(self.classes):\n",
    "            cls_path = os.path.join(data_dir, cls)\n",
    "            if not os.path.exists(cls_path):\n",
    "                continue\n",
    "            \n",
    "            for filename in os.listdir(cls_path):\n",
    "                if filename.lower().endswith(('.png', '.jpg', '.jpeg')):\n",
    "                    self.image_paths.append(os.path.join(cls_path, filename))\n",
    "                    self.labels.append(idx)\n",
    "                    \n",
    "        print(f\"Loaded {len(self.image_paths)} ECG images across {len(self.classes)} diagnostic classes.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __len__(self):\n",
    "        return len(self.image_paths)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n",
    "        img_path = self.image_paths[idx]\n",
    "        label = self.labels[idx]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Run advanced CV preprocessing\n",
    "        preprocessed = preprocess_ecg_image(img_path)\n",
    "        if preprocessed is None:\n",
    "            # Fallback to random black image if read fails\n",
    "            preprocessed = np.zeros((224, 224, 3), dtype=np.uint8)\n",
    "            \n",
    "        # Convert to PIL for standard transforms\n",
    "        pil_img = Image.fromarray(preprocessed)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        if self.transform:\n",
    "            pil_img = self.transform(pil_img)\n",
    "            \n",
    "        return pil_img, label"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 📸 4. Stage 3: Deep Feature Extraction (InceptionV3 Backbone)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class InceptionFeatureExtractor:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, device):\n",
    "        self.device = device\n",
    "        # Load pre-trained Inception V3\n",
    "        self.model = models.inception_v3(weights=models.Inception_V3_Weights.DEFAULT)\n",
    "        self.model.aux_logits = False # Disable auxiliary classifier output\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Remove final FC layer (2048 units)\n",
    "        self.model.fc = nn.Identity()\n",
    "        self.model = self.model.to(self.device)\n",
    "        self.model.eval()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Preprocessing normalization matching ImageNet values\n",
    "        self.transform = transforms.Compose([\n",
    "            transforms.ToTensor(),\n",
    "            transforms.Normalize([0.485, 0.456, 0.406], [0.229, 0.224, 0.225])\n",
    "        ])\n",
    "\n",
    "    def extract_all(self, dataset):\n",
    "        loader = DataLoader(dataset, batch_size=32, shuffle=False, num_workers=0)\n",
    "        features_list = []\n",
    "        labels_list = []\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(\"🚀 Extracting deep InceptionV3 representations...\")\n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            for inputs, labels in loader:\n",
    "                inputs = inputs.to(self.device)\n",
    "                # shape: [batch, 2048]\n",
    "                feats = self.model(inputs)\n",
    "                features_list.append(feats.cpu().numpy())\n",
    "                labels_list.append(labels.numpy())\n",
    "                \n",
    "        return np.concatenate(features_list, axis=0), np.concatenate(labels_list, axis=0)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🦈 5. Stage 4: Binary White Shark Optimization (WSO-LDA)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class BinaryWSOLDA:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Implements a Binary White Shark Optimization algorithm using a Linear\n",
    "    Discriminant Analysis validation metric as a fitness score.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_sharks=15, max_iter=20, alpha=0.99):\n",
    "        self.num_sharks = num_sharks\n",
    "        self.max_iter = max_iter\n",
    "        self.alpha = alpha  # Weighting factor between accuracy and sparsity\n",
    "\n",
    "    def fitness(self, mask, X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val):\n",
    "        selected_indices = np.where(mask == 1)[0]\n",
    "        if len(selected_indices) == 0:\n",
    "            return 999.0  # Heavy penalty for selecting no features\n",
    "            \n",
    "        X_tr = X_train[:, selected_indices]\n",
    "        X_va = X_val[:, selected_indices]\n",
    "        \n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            # Perform LDA classification\n",
    "            lda = LinearDiscriminantAnalysis()\n",
    "            lda.fit(X_tr, y_train)\n",
    "            preds = lda.predict(X_va)\n",
    "            error = 1.0 - accuracy_score(y_val, preds)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Sparsity penalty (minimize active features)\n",
    "            sparsity = len(selected_indices) / len(mask)\n",
    "            fit = self.alpha * error + (1 - self.alpha) * sparsity\n",
    "            return fit\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            return 999.0\n",
    "\n",
    "    def optimize(self, X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val):\n",
    "        num_features = X_train.shape[1]\n",
    "        print(f\"🦈 Starting WSO-LDA feature selection over {num_features} deep features...\")\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Initialize population of sharks (binary masks of shape [num_sharks, num_features])\n",
    "        sharks = np.random.randint(2, size=(self.num_sharks, num_features))\n",
    "        velocities = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=(self.num_sharks, num_features))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        best_mask = None\n",
    "        best_fitness = 999.0\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Odor momentum parameters\n",
    "        c1, c2 = 1.5, 1.5\n",
    "        mu = 0.8\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for iteration in range(self.max_iter):\n",
    "            for i in range(self.num_sharks):\n",
    "                fit = self.fitness(sharks[i], X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val)\n",
    "                \n",
    "                if fit < best_fitness:\n",
    "                    best_fitness = fit\n",
    "                    best_mask = copy.deepcopy(sharks[i])\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Update velocities and sharks positions based on odor tracking\n",
    "            prey = best_mask\n",
    "            for i in range(self.num_sharks):\n",
    "                r1, r2 = np.random.rand(), np.random.rand()\n",
    "                \n",
    "                # WSO Velocity equation\n",
    "                velocities[i] = mu * (velocities[i] + c1 * r1 * (best_mask - sharks[i]) + c2 * r2 * (prey - sharks[i]))\n",
    "                \n",
    "                # Sigmoid transfer function to project to binary space\n",
    "                sigmoid = 1 / (1 + np.exp(-velocities[i]))\n",
    "                sharks[i] = (np.random.rand(num_features) < sigmoid).astype(int)\n",
    "                \n",
    "            print(f\"   Iteration {iteration+1}/{self.max_iter} | Best Fitness: {best_fitness:.4f} | Selected features: {np.sum(best_mask)}/{num_features}\")\n",
    "            \n",
    "        return best_mask"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🕸️ 6. Stage 5: Custom Hybrid ANN Structure (HANN)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class HybridECGANN(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, input_dim, hidden_dim1=256, hidden_dim2=128, hidden_dim3=64):\n",
    "        super(HybridECGANN, self).__init__()\n",
    "        # Multilayer MLP head matching the strategy diagram\n",
    "        self.network = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(input_dim, hidden_dim1),\n",
    "            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden_dim1),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Dropout(0.3),\n",
    "            \n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim1, hidden_dim2),\n",
    "            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden_dim2),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            nn.Dropout(0.3),\n",
    "            \n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim2, hidden_dim3),\n",
    "            nn.BatchNorm1d(hidden_dim3),\n",
    "            nn.ReLU(),\n",
    "            \n",
    "            nn.Linear(hidden_dim3, 4)  # 4 ECG Output classes\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        return self.network(x)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def get_weights(self):\n",
    "        w = []\n",
    "        for name, param in self.named_parameters():\n",
    "            w.extend(param.detach().cpu().numpy().flatten())\n",
    "        return np.array(w)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def set_weights(self, flat_weights):\n",
    "        pointer = 0\n",
    "        for name, param in self.named_parameters():\n",
    "            num_el = param.numel()\n",
    "            arr = np.array(flat_weights[pointer:pointer+num_el]).reshape(param.shape)\n",
    "            param.data = torch.FloatTensor(arr)\n",
    "            pointer += num_el"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🐺 7. Stage 5: Multi-Objective Spotted Hyena Optimization (MOSHO)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class MOSHO:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Spotted Hyena meta-heuristic optimizer designed to minimize both cross-entropy loss\n",
    "    and False Negative Rate (FNR) to maximize clinical safety on heart disease prediction.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_hyenas=10, max_iter=25):\n",
    "        self.num_hyenas = num_hyenas\n",
    "        self.max_iter = max_iter\n",
    "        \n",
    "    def evaluate_clinical_metrics(self, weights, model, X, y):\n",
    "        # Inject flat parameters\n",
    "        model.set_weights(weights)\n",
    "        model.eval()\n",
    "        \n",
    "        inputs = torch.FloatTensor(X)\n",
    "        labels = torch.LongTensor(y)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "            outputs = model(inputs)\n",
    "            criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n",
    "            loss = criterion(outputs, labels).item()\n",
    "            \n",
    "            preds = torch.argmax(outputs, dim=1).numpy()\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Calculate False Negatives for Myocardial Infarction (Class index 2)\n",
    "            # MI (Class 2) vs others\n",
    "            binary_y = (y == 2).astype(int)\n",
    "            binary_preds = (preds == 2).astype(int)\n",
    "            \n",
    "            recall = recall_score(binary_y, binary_preds, zero_division=0)\n",
    "            fnr = 1.0 - recall\n",
    "            \n",
    "        return loss, fnr\n",
    "\n",
    "    def optimize(self, model, X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val):\n",
    "        print(\"🐺 Starting MOSHO multi-objective neural network parameter search...\")\n",
    "        sample_weights = model.get_weights()\n",
    "        dim = len(sample_weights)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Initialize Spotted Hyenas population\n",
    "        hyenas = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=(self.num_hyenas, dim))\n",
    "        best_hyena = None\n",
    "        best_loss = 999.0\n",
    "        best_fnr = 999.0\n",
    "        \n",
    "        for iteration in range(self.max_iter):\n",
    "            a = 2.0 - (iteration * (2.0 / self.max_iter)) # Linearly decreasing encircling variable\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Evaluate all agents\n",
    "            for i in range(self.num_hyenas):\n
    "                loss, fnr = self.evaluate_clinical_metrics(hyenas[i], model, X_val, y_val)\n",
    "                score = 0.5 * loss + 0.5 * fnr # Multi-objective balance\n",
    "                \n",
    "                if score < (0.5 * best_loss + 0.5 * best_fnr):\n",
    "                    best_loss = loss\n",
    "                    best_fnr = fnr\n",
    "                    best_hyena = copy.deepcopy(hyenas[i])\n",
    "            \n",
    "            # Update hyena coordinates using group encircling\n",
    "            for i in range(self.num_hyenas):\n",
    "                r1, r2 = np.random.rand(), np.random.rand()\n",
    "                A = 2 * a * r1 - a\n",
    "                C = 2 * r2\n",
    "                \n",
    "                D_h = np.abs(C * best_hyena - hyenas[i])\n",
    "                P_k = best_hyena - A * D_h\n",
    "                hyenas[i] = (hyenas[i] + P_k) / 2.0 # Cluster average updates\n",
    "                \n",
    "            print(f\"   Iteration {iteration+1}/{self.max_iter} | Validation Cross-Entropy: {best_loss:.4f} | Validation MI False Negative Rate: {best_fnr*100:.2f}%\")\n",
    "            \n",
    "        return best_hyena"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 🚀 8. Pipeline Execution, Evaluation, and ONNX Export"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "print(\"🫀 EXECUTING END-TO-END IoMT ECG CLASSIFICATION PIPELINE\")\n",
    "print(\"=\"*70)\n",
    "\n",
    "DATA_DIR = \"ecg_data\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(DATA_DIR):\n",
    "    print(f\"Error: '{DATA_DIR}' folder not found. Please place this notebook in your project root.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    # 1. Load Dataset\n",
    "    extractor = InceptionFeatureExtractor(device=DEVICE)\n",
    "    dataset = ECGDataset(data_dir=DATA_DIR, transform=extractor.transform)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 2. Extract Deep features\n",
    "    X, y = extractor.extract_all(dataset)\n",
    "    print(f\"Successfully extracted feature shape: {X.shape} | labels shape: {y.shape}\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Train-test splitting\n",
    "    shuffled_indices = np.random.permutation(len(X))\n",
    "    split_point = int(0.7 * len(X))\n",
    "    \n",
    "    X_train, y_train = X[shuffled_indices[:split_point]], y[shuffled_indices[:split_point]]\n",
    "    X_val, y_val = X[shuffled_indices[split_point:]], y[shuffled_indices[split_point:]]\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 3. Apply WSO-LDA Feature Selection\n",
    "    wso = BinaryWSOLDA(num_sharks=8, max_iter=10, alpha=0.98)\n",
    "    best_mask = wso.optimize(X_train, y_train, X_val, y_val)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    selected_features = np.where(best_mask == 1)[0]\n",
    "    X_train_sel = X_train[:, selected_features]\n",
    "    X_val_sel = X_val[:, selected_features]\n",
    "    input_dim = len(selected_features)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nOptimal feature dimensions: {input_dim}-D (Reduced from 2048-D)\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 4. Train HANN Classifier via MOSHO Weight Optimization\n",
    "    hann = HybridECGANN(input_dim=input_dim).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "    mosho = MOSHO(num_hyenas=8, max_iter=15)\n",
    "    best_weights = mosho.optimize(hann, X_train_sel, y_train, X_val_sel, y_val)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Set final optimized weights\n",
    "    hann.set_weights(best_weights)\n",
    "    hann = hann.cpu()  # Move to CPU for exporting\n",
    "    hann.eval()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # 5. Final Metrics Evaluation\n",
    "    with torch.no_grad():\n",
    "        test_inputs = torch.FloatTensor(X_val_sel)\n",
    "        logits = hann(test_inputs)\n",
    "        probs = torch.softmax(logits, dim=1).numpy()\n",
    "        preds = np.argmax(probs, axis=1)\n",
    "        \n",
    "    accuracy = accuracy_score(y_val, preds) * 100\n",
    "    sensitivity = recall_score(y_val, preds, average='macro', zero_division=0) * 100\n",
    "    f1 = f1_score(y_val, preds, average='macro', zero_division=0) * 100\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\"*40)\n",
    "    print(\"📊 FINAL DIAGNOSTIC EVALUATION RESULTS\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\"*40)\n",
    "    print(f\"Accuracy Score:  {accuracy:.2f}%\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Sensitivity:     {sensitivity:.2f}% (True Positive Rate)\")\n",
    "    print(f\"Macro F1-Score:  {f1:.2f}%\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\"*40)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # ==================================================================\n",
    "    # 📦 9. COMBINED PIPELINE ONNX EXPORT\n",
    "    # ==================================================================\n",
    "    print(\"\\nCreating unified wrapper for complete ONNX export (CNN + HANN)... \")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    class CompleteECGClassifierONNX(nn.Module):\n",
    "        def __init__(self, cnn_backbone, feature_mask, hann_classifier):\n",
    "            super(CompleteECGClassifierONNX, self).__init__()\n",
    "            self.cnn = cnn_backbone\n",
    "            self.register_buffer('mask', torch.LongTensor(np.where(feature_mask == 1)[0]))\n",
    "            self.hann = hann_classifier\n",
    "            \n",
    "        def forward(self, x):\n",
    "            # 1. Spatial InceptionV3 forward pass\n",
    "            features = self.cnn(x)\n",
    "            # 2. Extract selected features\n",
    "            selected_features = torch.index_select(features, 1, self.mask)\n",
    "            # 3. Classify using HANN\n",
    "            logits = self.hann(selected_features)\n",
    "            return logits\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Instantiate combined wrapper\n",
    "    combined_model = CompleteECGClassifierONNX(extractor.model.cpu(), best_mask, hann)\n",
    "    combined_model.eval()\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Create a dummy image input [batch, 3, 224, 224] for tracing\n",
    "    dummy_input = torch.randn(1, 3, 224, 224)\n",
    "    \n",
    "    print(\"Exporting unified model to 'ecg_model.onnx'...\")\n",
    "    torch.onnx.export(\n",
    "        combined_model,\n",
    "        dummy_input,\n",
    "        \"ecg_model.onnx\",\n",
    "        export_params=True,\n",
    "        opset_version=15,\n",
